invariant: INV-14
file: tls.c
catches: webpki_session_test
reason: ch_connect compares two offered protocol names by address rather
  than by their bytes, so a config that offers the same name twice from
  two buffers passes. The server's selection then names two indices, and
  ch_tls.alpn_selected reports one, so a caller reading it cannot tell
  which entry the server meant. bin/webpki_session_test's repeated-name
  row offers the bytes of "h2" a second time from another address, and
  objects.

--- old
        if (cfg->alpn_protocols[i].name_len == cfg->alpn_protocols[j].name_len &&
            ct_memeq(cfg->alpn_protocols[i].name, cfg->alpn_protocols[j].name,
                     cfg->alpn_protocols[i].name_len)) {
--- new
        if (cfg->alpn_protocols[i].name == cfg->alpn_protocols[j].name) {
